Fix render_ipynb_layout building a Div from a pandoc.Blocks value.

The pandoc.Div() constructor in pandoc 3.x rejects a Blocks-typed value
("Block, list of Blocks, or compatible element expected, got Blocks"),
which breaks any figure that uses layout-ncol / fig-subcap during the
manuscript embed pass.

Use pandoc.List() instead, which Div() accepts.

--- a/share/filters/main.lua
+++ b/share/filters/main.lua
@@ -23697,7 +23697,7 @@ local function render_ipynb_layout(layout)
   end
   -- outer panel to contain css and figure panel
   local attr = pandoc.Attr(layout.identifier or "", layout.classes or {}, layout.attributes or {})
-  local panel_content = pandoc.Blocks({})
+  local panel_content = pandoc.List()
   -- layout
   for i, row in ipairs(layout.layout) do

